<%# Owner-only analytics dashboard. Aggregates only, off the denormalized hujahs
    counters — no per-voter data anywhere.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Hoojah 2026, Slice 2026 Phase 4.6) — mockup "Analytics · dashboard"
    ~lines 1456-1510, restyling Slice 9 Task 4.7's version.
    docs/design-system/components/analytics/*.prompt.md for the two chips and the bars
    still applies to the shapes; this pass changes tone, not structure.

    HEADER: `shared/_screen_header` replaces the earlier `shared/navbar` + hand-rolled
    `<h1>`. The mockup draws this screen as a drill-down (back arrow + title bar), the
    same chrome `debates/new` uses, not the persistent top-level nav every feed/list page
    keeps — this page is reached from the avatar menu, one level down from the feed, so
    `back:` returns to `root_path`. That is also why the page title moves off the
    `blocks/index`-style `text-lg font-medium` idiom documented below: `_screen_header`
    owns its own `<h1>` (`text-base font-bold text-ink`), and duplicating a second title
    directly under it would be a second heading for one screen.

    FOLLOWERS KPI (Task 4.6): computed in the controller as
    `current_user.followers.count`, NOT inside `UserAnalytics` — see that model's header
    comment and `AnalyticsController#show`. `UserAnalytics` reads only `hujahs`; the
    follower count is `users`+`follows` and stays entirely outside it, which is also why
    it is a separate "stat" partial call passed `@followers_count` rather than a value
    pulled off `@analytics`.

    NO delta/percentage-change chip and NO 7-day chart. The mockup draws both ("↑ 12%
    this week", a bar-per-weekday sparkline); this app has no backing time-series for
    either — `UserAnalytics` and the followers count are both live point-in-time reads,
    not snapshots. Fabricating a trend off a single reading would be fictional data on a
    page whose whole point is real, denormalized counters. Deferred until there is an
    actual snapshot job to read from.

    TOP HOOJAH: the user's own top-level hoojah with the most total votes, rendered with
    `_distribution_bar`'s `stacked:` form (see that partial's comment). Ties and the
    "no hoojahs yet" case both fall through to `nil` via `max_by`, so the card only
    renders when there is a hoojah to show — no separate empty state needed here, since
    the section below already carries `ui/_empty_state` for "no hoojahs at all".

    The per-hoojah `_distribution_bar` list below is UNCHANGED (the row form, the k=3
    suppression, the empty state) — this pass adds to the page, it does not replace that
    section. %>
<%= render "shared/screen_header", title: "Your dashboard", back: root_path %>

<main class="max-w-xl mx-auto px-4 py-6">
  <div class="flex gap-3 mb-4">
    <%= render "stat", label: "Total votes received", value: @analytics.total_votes_received %>
    <%= render "stat", label: "Followers", value: @followers_count %>
  </div>

  <% top = @analytics.distributions.max_by(&:total) %>
  <% if top %>
    <%= render "distribution_bar", dist: top, stacked: true, heading: "Top hoojah" %>
  <% end %>

  <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-2 mb-3 mt-2">Your hoojahs</h2>
  <% if @analytics.distributions.any? %>
    <%= render partial: "distribution_bar", collection: @analytics.distributions, as: :dist %>
  <% else %>
    <%= render "ui/empty_state", message: "You haven't posted any hoojahs yet", icon: "bar-chart-3" %>
  <% end %>
</main>
